# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Talon — the one config file. ./dev.sh reads this, the Go server loads it,
# the frontend's API URL is derived from it. Change a value, run ./dev.sh.
#
# `./dev.sh`          starts backend + frontend
# `./dev.sh stop`     stops both
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── The model ── Swap these three lines to change what builds your apps.
# Any OpenRouter model works: AI_PROTOCOL=openai, AI_BASE_URL as below,
# AI_MODEL as the model slug. Anthropic's native API also works
# (AI_PROTOCOL=anthropic, AI_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com).
AI_PROTOCOL=openai
AI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
AI_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-YOUR-OPENROUTER-KEY
# ── The model ── Any OpenRouter model slug works, but a free route has to
# clear one bar before it's usable here: a full plan-sized generation (~2k
# output tokens) must finish inside OpenRouter's ~5-minute provider window,
# not just a one-line reply. stealth/union-alpha is free and fails that bar —
# a trivial reply takes 60-90s and a real plan returns 502
# provider_unavailable after 2m45s. nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free clears
# it: 1M context, a full plan in ~20s. Verify a candidate with a plan-sized
# request before trusting it.
AI_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free
# Used for cheap paths (titles, summaries). Falls back to AI_MODEL when empty.
AI_MODEL_CHEAP=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free
# How the router treats the model: strong | fast. Strong = full reasoning for
# plans and builds. Only override if you know the model's tier.
AI_MODEL_TIER=strong

# Gateway pacing: the minimum gap between model calls. OpenRouter's free tier
# rate-limits hard (~8 req/min → 8s); a paid model can take 0s or empty
# (unset) to disable pacing entirely.
AI_MIN_REQUEST_INTERVAL=0s

# ── Hosts ── The address browsers and phones use to reach this studio.
# PUBLIC_HOST is your LAN IP for on-device testing. The frontend derives its
# API URL from it (PUBLIC_HOST:PORT), so phones and LAN browsers all hit the
# same backend.
PUBLIC_HOST=YOUR-LAN-IP
# WEB_ORIGIN is where the WEB APP lives — the OAuth hand-off redirects here
# and the CORS allowlist admits it. It is NOT the API; do not point the
# frontend at it. Override the API origin with NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL instead.
WEB_ORIGIN=http://YOUR-LAN-IP:3000

# ── Ports ── PORT is the backend; FRONTEND_PORT is the web server.
# Both default when empty (8080 / 3000).
PORT=8080
FRONTEND_PORT=3000

# ── Paths ── Where the DB and scrcpy server live. Both default when empty.
# DB_PATH=./talon.db  (relative to backend/)
SCRCPY_SERVER=./scrcpy-server.jar

# ── Session signing ── Change this for any real deployment.
JWT_SECRET=YOUR-JWT-SECRET

# ── OAuth ── Sign-in is GitHub and Google. Both are required for login to
# work; register an app at github.com/settings/developers and
# console.cloud.google.com and paste the IDs here.
AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=YOUR-GITHUB-CLIENT-ID
AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR-GITHUB-CLIENT-SECRET

AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR-GOOGLE-CLIENT-ID
AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR-GOOGLE-CLIENT-SECRET

# ── Push (optional) ── OneSignal for build-notifications. Leave empty to
# skip push; nothing else depends on it.
ONESIGNAL_APP_ID=YOUR-ONESIGNAL-APP-ID
ONESIGNAL_REST_API_KEY=YOUR-ONESIGNAL-REST-KEY

# ── Attachments (optional) ── Chat images go to Cloudflare R2 when all four
# are set; otherwise (and always for .md docs) they stay on local disk.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=YOUR-CLOUDFLARE-ACCOUNT-ID
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=YOUR-R2-ACCESS-KEY
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=YOUR-R2-SECRET-KEY
# R2_BUCKET=talon-attachments
# R2_PREFIX=attachments
